1
00:00:05,867 --> 00:00:07,200
[This drama is a work of fiction]

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,633
[All scenes involving animals and children
were filmed in compliance with regulations]

3
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:54,200
Darn!

4
00:01:01,633 --> 00:01:04,300
Once upon a time,

5
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:08,700
in a cozy little town with beautiful scenery,

6
00:01:10,733 --> 00:01:15,267
there lived a dependable father
named Jae Hong,

7
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:21,767
a kind and gentle mother named Kyung Hee,

8
00:01:22,667 --> 00:01:27,500
and their dutiful daughter, Ye Ji,
who never gave her parents a moment's worry.

9
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:50,600
As long as they had each other,

10
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:55,033
the three needed no treasure in the world.

11
00:01:55,033 --> 00:01:58,167
- Honey.
- Mommy.

12
00:01:58,167 --> 00:02:00,433
Let's get filthy rich.

13
00:02:01,867 --> 00:02:05,000
Yeah, honey. Let's make it big.

14
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,167
[Emergency Medical Center]

15
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:14,500
And so, the couple decided
they were going to make it big.

16
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:15,633
[The Rooftop Pool Is
Suddenly Open for Business]

17
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:18,233
[Captain Park on the Go, 18 Subscribers]

18
00:02:20,733 --> 00:02:22,567
[Easy DIY Wallpapering for Beginners]

19
00:02:22,567 --> 00:02:24,567
[Super Easy DIY Wine Crate Mood Light]

20
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:26,100
[Super Easy DIY Doorknob Replacement]

21
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:28,633
[2.3K, 2.4K]

22
00:02:28,633 --> 00:02:29,733
[Turn Old Hangers into a Clothes Rack]

23
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:32,133
[Captain Park on the Go]

24
00:02:32,133 --> 00:02:34,867
[1M Views, Captain Park on the Go]
Yes, crew. Hello, this is Captain Park.

25
00:02:34,867 --> 00:02:38,733
[Captain Park's Family Moves into a New Home]
Today, we've got some amazing news.

26
00:02:38,733 --> 00:02:40,267
Yes, thanks to all of you,

27
00:02:40,267 --> 00:02:43,400
we finally made it
out of our rooftop apartment.

28
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:45,733
Thank you.

29
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:47,333
What are you doing, honey?

30
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:48,867
Shall we give our crew a deep bow?

31
00:02:48,867 --> 00:02:49,900
- Sounds good.
- Yeah.

32
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:50,900
Everyone!

33
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:52,933
- Thank you so much.
- We truly appreciate it.

34
00:02:52,933 --> 00:02:55,767
- Thank you.
- We'll keep working hard and live well.

35
00:02:55,767 --> 00:02:57,833
- Thank you.
- Thank you!

36
00:02:57,833 --> 00:02:59,733
- Thank you!
- Thank you, everyone!

37
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:02,967
Yes, this is Captain Park, everyone.
I've got some great news today.

38
00:03:02,967 --> 00:03:05,533
This is our new home.

39
00:03:05,533 --> 00:03:06,967
It's a brand-new apartment.

40
00:03:06,967 --> 00:03:10,733
We've got views on both sides. A city view!

41
00:03:10,733 --> 00:03:12,233
Honey, why does a new apartment
smell so good?

42
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:15,233
I love it. I love it. I love it.

43
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:16,833
It's all thanks to you.

44
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,267
Just like we announced earlier,

45
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:21,367
we've finished remodeling our new kitchen.

46
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:24,467
- Wow, it looks incredible.
- Isn't this metal panel really dazzling?

47
00:03:24,467 --> 00:03:25,900
Thank you all so much.

48
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,600
It's all thanks to you!

49
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:28,633
Your turn, honey.

50
00:03:28,633 --> 00:03:29,733
- Yes, everyone!
- Let's bow.

51
00:03:29,733 --> 00:03:33,933
- We owe it all to you.
- Thank you so much, everyone.

52
00:03:42,533 --> 00:03:44,367
Yeah, everyone! Captain Park here.

53
00:03:44,367 --> 00:03:46,067
As we previewed today,

54
00:03:46,067 --> 00:03:47,767
- for the first time to our crew members,
- I'm not going.

55
00:03:47,767 --> 00:03:51,300
here's the first look
at Captain Park's new home.

56
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:55,433
Eun Bin, Ye Ji, what are you doing?

57
00:03:55,433 --> 00:03:56,867
Come bow to our viewers.

58
00:03:56,867 --> 00:03:59,467
Seriously? That's embarrassing.

59
00:03:59,467 --> 00:04:02,533
Hello, I'm Cha Eun Bin!

60
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:06,067
What's so embarrassing about it?
I'm doing it too, okay? Come on.

61
00:04:06,067 --> 00:04:07,667
Well, you should.

62
00:04:07,667 --> 00:04:10,300
Your biggest hit is Mom's YouTube channel.

63
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:13,800
Why would my biggest work
be your mom's YouTube channel?

64
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:16,633
I've got plenty of great work to my name.

65
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:18,300
Be careful, be careful.

66
00:04:19,733 --> 00:04:23,033
This is all for your beloved mom, Ye Ji.

67
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:24,533
What did I always tell you?

68
00:04:24,533 --> 00:04:27,367
If you love someone,
you'll do anything for them.

69
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:29,000
That's what really makes someone cool.

70
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,567
Okay, Ye Ji?

71
00:04:30,567 --> 00:04:32,733
Besides, let's be honest.

72
00:04:32,733 --> 00:04:37,900
We got this amazing house
thanks to your mom. Isn't that true?

73
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,500
That's true.

74
00:04:40,167 --> 00:04:42,600
- I'm going crazy, seriously...
- What? What's wrong, honey?

75
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:44,133
Why on earth am I crying?

76
00:04:44,133 --> 00:04:46,467
You're crying? You shouldn't be crying.

77
00:04:46,467 --> 00:04:49,433
Not on a happy day like this. Cheer up!

78
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,267
Ugh, seriously...

79
00:04:52,267 --> 00:04:54,433
What's gotten into them?

80
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:00,467
If you don't want us getting kicked out,
hurry up and bow.

81
00:05:00,467 --> 00:05:02,233
Come on, Ye Ji.

82
00:05:03,367 --> 00:05:05,467
Crew members, thank you so much.

83
00:05:05,467 --> 00:05:08,500
We'll make the most of this!

84
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:10,500
- Bow.
- Thank you!

85
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,333
- Thank you!
- Thank you.

86
00:05:15,967 --> 00:05:17,033
Cut!

87
00:05:17,033 --> 00:05:20,633
Great. Nice work, everyone.

88
00:05:20,633 --> 00:05:21,900
- Did we get everything?
- Good job.

89
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:23,567
Good job!

90
00:05:55,267 --> 00:05:58,767
[Presented to "Captain Park on the Go"
for Passing 1,000,000 Subscribers, YouTube]

91
00:06:43,533 --> 00:06:49,100
[Episode 1, Cheating Husband A]

92
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:56,933
Connecting to Ye Ji's phone.

93
00:06:56,933 --> 00:06:59,600
Connecting Ye Ji's CarPlay.

94
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:00,833
[The Day Captain Park's Family Moves
into a Luxury Single-Family Home]

95
00:07:00,833 --> 00:07:01,833
[You're cool, Captain Park!
Huge congratulations!]

96
00:07:01,833 --> 00:07:03,633
[It's absolutely gorgeous.
Congratulations, Captain Park!]

97
00:07:03,633 --> 00:07:04,667
[8:49 Why does Ye Ji look so cool?
I almost fell for a middle schooler]

98
00:07:04,667 --> 00:07:05,700
[Wow, as expected of my role model.
Her fashion sense is insane]

99
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:06,700
[As expected of Captain Park!
Congratulations!]

100
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:08,500
[9:01 Watching Ye Ji's smile on repeat
for the 249,837th time]

101
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:10,167
[I love Captain Park's family so much,
I wish I were Captain Park's daughter]

102
00:07:17,933 --> 00:07:19,900
Come on, let's go already.

103
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:22,000
Your only daughter is going to be late
for her first day of school.

104
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Yeah, we've still got time.

105
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,033
The girl in the house across from us
is in your school and grade.

106
00:07:27,033 --> 00:07:30,033
Wouldn't it be nice
to start off with a friend?

107
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:33,467
Just because she's my age and lives
next door doesn't mean we'll be friends.

108
00:07:33,467 --> 00:07:35,300
Oh, there she is!

109
00:07:40,033 --> 00:07:41,800
Min Seo!

110
00:07:43,167 --> 00:07:46,667
Are you sure you don't want a ride?

111
00:07:47,367 --> 00:07:49,900
- Hello!
- Hello!

112
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,467
- Oh, yeah.
- We moved into the house across the street.

113
00:07:52,467 --> 00:07:54,233
- Hello.
- Yeah.

114
00:07:54,233 --> 00:07:57,000
Oh, you go to
Cheongnam Girls' Middle School too?

115
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:58,167
- Oh, hi.
- Perfect timing.

116
00:07:58,167 --> 00:08:01,000
We were just about to head to school.

117
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,100
Would you like a ride?

118
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:04,733
We should save gas and save time
in a country that doesn't produce oil.

119
00:08:04,733 --> 00:08:07,000
And it's good for the girls
to become friends.

120
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,567
Neighbors should help each other out.

121
00:08:08,567 --> 00:08:11,900
Thanks, but maybe not today.

122
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:17,200
Oh, how about
having a meal together on the weekend?

123
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:19,733
Just check with your husband and let us know.

124
00:08:19,733 --> 00:08:22,500
I'm actually a pretty good cook.

125
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,100
Oh, okay.

126
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:27,167
By the way, I guess your husband
left for work earlier.

127
00:08:31,633 --> 00:08:36,800
I never imagined someone
this famous would move in next door.

128
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:40,900
I know. We never imagined we'd end up
living in this neighborhood either.

129
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:43,500
It's all thanks to our Captain Park.

130
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,633
I see you film all over
different neighborhoods.

131
00:08:45,633 --> 00:08:48,633
Oh? Have you seen our YouTube channel?

132
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:50,900
Wait, are you one of our crew members
by any chance?

133
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:53,067
You're not going to do that here too,
are you?

134
00:08:53,067 --> 00:08:56,533
I'm just not used to
all the noise and commotion.

135
00:08:58,067 --> 00:08:59,667
Wait.

136
00:09:00,667 --> 00:09:03,300
I stopped by yesterday to drop this off,
but no one was home.

137
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:05,233
[Park Kyung Hee, CEO of the ZiP]
It's a housewarming rice cake.

138
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:09,067
You really went through a lot of trouble.

139
00:09:09,067 --> 00:09:11,933
People around here
don't usually do this kind of thing.

140
00:09:11,933 --> 00:09:14,867
You don't have to go to
all this trouble next time.

141
00:09:14,867 --> 00:09:16,567
Not at all.

142
00:09:18,367 --> 00:09:21,700
Sometimes too much thoughtfulness
can be a bit overwhelming.

143
00:09:22,967 --> 00:09:25,067
Min Seo, get in the car.

144
00:09:25,067 --> 00:09:27,400
Thank you for the ride.

145
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:36,333
Wow. That's insane.

146
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:39,333
What a load of crap, seriously.

147
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:42,533
That's why her own daughter
openly ignores her.

148
00:09:42,533 --> 00:09:46,133
"Sometimes too much thoughtfulness
can be a bit overwhelming."

149
00:09:46,133 --> 00:09:48,633
What a two-faced punk.

150
00:09:48,633 --> 00:09:50,733
Who does she think she is,
treating someone's kindness like garbage?

151
00:09:50,733 --> 00:09:51,933
That's what I'm saying.

152
00:09:51,933 --> 00:09:54,433
Honey, here. Pull.

153
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:56,433
So, Hong.

154
00:09:56,433 --> 00:09:59,233
Please stop wasting money on ugly brown cars
and start moving in better circles.

155
00:09:59,233 --> 00:10:04,400
That's the only way
people will stop looking down on you.

156
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:09,633
Honey, just the wrap on that car
cost five million won.

157
00:10:09,633 --> 00:10:12,433
And it's not brown. It's called "Rich Gold."

158
00:10:12,433 --> 00:10:14,633
What do you mean by "Rich Gold"?

159
00:10:14,633 --> 00:10:16,367
Is that some kind of pizza?

160
00:10:17,433 --> 00:10:19,967
She's definitely got a personality disorder.

161
00:10:19,967 --> 00:10:22,867
Otherwise, she's the daughter
of Cheongnam Hospital, a doctor,

162
00:10:22,867 --> 00:10:26,600
elegant, well... pretty, and classy.

163
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:30,267
She's got everything,
yet her husband still left her.

164
00:10:30,267 --> 00:10:33,267
But I heard they ran the hospital together
and got along well.

165
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:36,133
So that real estate agent
lied to us back then?

166
00:10:36,133 --> 00:10:38,400
Yeah, apparently it was all a lie.

167
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:40,700
I could tell just by the way
that woman acted.

168
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:43,067
So I grilled the real estate agent,

169
00:10:43,067 --> 00:10:44,867
and it turns out her husband

170
00:10:44,867 --> 00:10:48,367
abandoned the house, the hospital,
everything, and ran off.

171
00:10:48,367 --> 00:10:50,367
Apparently, the woman next door

172
00:10:50,367 --> 00:10:51,833
came running out barefoot,

173
00:10:51,833 --> 00:10:55,300
sobbing and grabbing his legs,
causing a huge scene.

174
00:10:56,367 --> 00:10:58,400
She acted so refined and classy,

175
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:01,767
but turns out she's a total mess.

176
00:11:02,633 --> 00:11:06,533
Anyway, they've been
separated for months now.

177
00:11:08,067 --> 00:11:09,100
[Ryu Ji Su: Thank you, oppa
Me: See you next time]

178
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:11,667
[We'll finally see each other tomorrow]
No wonder she looked so miserable.

179
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:13,867
What are you talking about?

180
00:11:13,867 --> 00:11:16,500
But why on earth is that woman like that?

181
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:19,500
Honey, ignore her! Just ignore her.

182
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:22,367
Neighbors being close?
Please. Don't bother with that nonsense.

183
00:11:22,367 --> 00:11:23,867
Like that's even a thing.

184
00:11:23,867 --> 00:11:28,400
From now on, even if she begs
to be friends, I'm done with her.

185
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:33,367
So, Hong, just completely
ignore her from now on.

186
00:11:33,367 --> 00:11:36,833
Okay, I'm not even going to
say hello to her anymore.

187
00:11:36,833 --> 00:11:39,633
Even if she greets me first,
I'll pretend I didn't see her.

188
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:45,200
But does the IR deck
really need this much text?

189
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,167
Yes, then I'll reorganize it
and send it over again.

190
00:11:47,167 --> 00:11:49,533
It's the DIY paint prototype samples
you mentioned before.

191
00:11:49,533 --> 00:11:51,033
Yes, number two.

192
00:11:51,033 --> 00:11:53,467
But the actual color
looks completely different.

193
00:11:53,467 --> 00:11:55,933
Check whether it's an issue with the product
or the display and let me know.

194
00:11:55,933 --> 00:11:56,933
Yes.

195
00:11:56,933 --> 00:11:59,667
- And here's the final thumbnail version.
- Yeah.

196
00:12:00,767 --> 00:12:02,633
Oh, it's too cluttered.

197
00:12:02,633 --> 00:12:06,033
Use version three as the base
and remove anything unnecessary.

198
00:12:06,033 --> 00:12:08,833
- This will be our first impression.
- Yes, I'll update it right away.

199
00:12:08,833 --> 00:12:12,000
This is the product
that will be featured in this episode.

200
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:16,133
We're planning to highlight that
it's waterproof, resistant to stains,

201
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:18,033
- and highly breathable.
- It's soft.

202
00:12:18,033 --> 00:12:21,767
Yes, since it's popular among families
with children and pets,

203
00:12:21,767 --> 00:12:23,167
we're thinking of
adding that concept as well.

204
00:12:23,167 --> 00:12:25,300
- Yes, sounds good.
- Captain Park!

205
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:27,633
Just a moment, just a moment.

206
00:12:28,467 --> 00:12:31,733
Info on Michelle Jung's associates!

207
00:12:32,633 --> 00:12:34,367
[Michelle Jung, provides support
and investments across various fields]

208
00:12:34,367 --> 00:12:36,567
[Director Ahn Won Seok of Cheongnam General]
I had a really hard time.

209
00:12:36,567 --> 00:12:37,728
[CEO Park Kyung Hee]
These days, even Korea doesn't invest

210
00:12:37,728 --> 00:12:40,100
based on connections.

211
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,633
She's only Michelle in name.

212
00:12:42,633 --> 00:12:48,033
Her mindset is completely stuck
in the past, like she never left Korea.

213
00:12:48,033 --> 00:12:49,867
I can't stand it, seriously.

214
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:55,067
Anyway, look into it. See if there's
anyone we can get an introduction to.

215
00:12:55,067 --> 00:12:58,300
Director Kwak,
you must've worked your tail off.

216
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:02,200
Still, even if it means dealing with this,
we need Michelle Jung's investment.

217
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:05,167
Her name alone will make
future investments easier to secure.

218
00:13:05,167 --> 00:13:08,367
[Director Joo Bo Sung, CEO Kim Ji Yeon]
We need investment to expand the business,

219
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:11,067
pay our employees,

220
00:13:11,067 --> 00:13:13,500
and finally ease some of the pressure.

221
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,567
This is driving me crazy, seriously.

222
00:13:20,567 --> 00:13:22,368
[Director Ahn Soo Jung, Dermatologist,
Her father's connection with Michelle Jung]

223
00:13:22,368 --> 00:13:24,100
[led her to volunteer with her often]

224
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:26,000
A billion won? Ten billion won?

225
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,600
Don't do this.

226
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:30,567
If money was what I cared about,
I would have never dated you, Ji Hoon.

227
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,333
I'll siphon off hundreds of millions,
even billions,

228
00:13:34,333 --> 00:13:38,433
from Han Jung Woo's townhouse
and bring it to you, Ji Hoon.

229
00:13:38,433 --> 00:13:40,800
But that's as far as you can go.

230
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:44,400
You can't be Ji Yeon's father.

231
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,100
Cut!

232
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,333
Yes, okay!

233
00:13:48,333 --> 00:13:50,900
Director, was my acting okay?

234
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:53,200
Yes, Ms. Ryu! That was great.

235
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:55,500
I almost cried, seriously.

236
00:13:57,467 --> 00:14:01,633
Wow, idols these days
are all pretty good actors,

237
00:14:01,633 --> 00:14:04,533
but how is she so consistently bad?

238
00:14:04,533 --> 00:14:08,167
If she could act well too,
she'd be a world star by now.

239
00:14:08,167 --> 00:14:10,267
Mr. Kang, please teach her a bit.

240
00:14:10,267 --> 00:14:12,467
When it comes to acting,
who else but Kang Tae Han?

241
00:14:12,467 --> 00:14:14,867
Come on, don't say that. No, no.

242
00:14:14,867 --> 00:14:18,200
The god of acting,
the very definition of excellence!

243
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:19,233
Well, then I...

244
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:22,100
