522
00:30:38,867 --> 00:30:41,900
Yeah. And it's better
coming here just the two of us.

523
00:30:41,900 --> 00:30:45,200
These are all flowering trees. Imagine
how beautiful it'll be when they bloom.

524
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:47,767
And the air is definitely different.

525
00:30:47,767 --> 00:30:48,767
- Different?
- Yeah.

526
00:30:48,767 --> 00:30:51,367
- Just getting out of Seoul feels different.
- Right.

527
00:30:51,367 --> 00:30:54,133
Huh? What is this?

528
00:30:54,133 --> 00:30:56,367
What is it? Is it a drain?

529
00:30:58,767 --> 00:31:01,667
- Why is something like this here?
- Honey, Hong, look at this.

530
00:31:01,667 --> 00:31:02,800
What is this?

531
00:31:02,800 --> 00:31:04,133
Huh?

532
00:31:04,133 --> 00:31:06,667
- Open it.
- What is it? What is this?

533
00:31:16,600 --> 00:31:18,500
Honey, hold this for me!

534
00:31:22,567 --> 00:31:24,367
Be careful, be careful!

535
00:31:25,367 --> 00:31:27,100
What is this?

536
00:31:27,867 --> 00:31:31,400
But the realtor never mentioned this.

537
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:33,633
Hong, go inside and check it out.

538
00:31:34,867 --> 00:31:36,733
Me?

539
00:31:36,733 --> 00:31:38,400
Yeah.

540
00:31:43,067 --> 00:31:45,400
A man should go in.

541
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:49,733
What is this place?

542
00:31:52,533 --> 00:31:54,200
Spiderwebs.

543
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,633
What is it?

544
00:32:05,267 --> 00:32:07,433
Why is everything so rotten?

545
00:32:12,333 --> 00:32:14,300
It's like some kind of storage room.

546
00:32:14,300 --> 00:32:16,000
Oh, really?

547
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:17,100
What? What? What?

548
00:32:17,100 --> 00:32:19,333
- Wait, hold on!
- What, what? What is it?

549
00:32:41,067 --> 00:32:43,000
